Project Title
Auto Ticket Classification using Flow Designer
2. Project Objective
The objective is to develop an automated ticket classification system using ServiceNow Flow Designer to reduce manual effort and improve the efficiency of the school IT helpdesk.
3. Technology Used
Platform: ServiceNow
Automation Tool: Flow Designer
Database/Table: Incident WorkFlow
Application Scope: Global
Update Set: Project Update Set
4. Project Activities
Activity
Description
Requirement Analysis
Identify the helpdesk problem and requirements
Project Design
Design the table, fields, categories and workflow
Table Creation
Create the Incident WorkFlow table
Field Creation
Create required ticket fields
Dependency Setup
Configure Category and Subcategory dependency
Flow Development
Create the automated classification flow
Notification Setup
Configure email notification
Testing
Test different ticket scenarios
Documentation
Prepare project documentation
Deployment
Complete and export the Update Set
5. Classification Plan
The flow will classify tickets using keywords in the ticket description:
Wi-Fi / Network → Network → Wi-Fi
Projector / Hardware → Hardware → Projector
Password / Login / Forgot Password → Access → Forgot Password
Slow / Hanging / Slow Computer → Performance → Slow Computer
6. Testing Plan
The system will be tested using different ticket descriptions.
Test Case 1
Short Description: WiFi not working in library
Expected Result:
Category: Network
Subcategory: Wi-Fi
Email notification sent to Caller
Test Case 2
Short Description: Projector not turning on
Expected Result:
Category: Hardware
Subcategory: Projector
Email notification sent to Caller
7. Expected Outcome
The planned system will provide automatic ticket classification, dependent Category and Subcategory selection, and email notification. This will reduce manual effort and provide a structured process for handling school IT helpdesk requests.
